# Hyperbaric oxygen therapy (G0277, 99183), from Medicare NCD 20.29, with the codes of the Medicare Claims Processing
# Manual chapter 32 section 30.1. Status draft: awaiting clinical sign-off (vaglio signoff). Every clause is quoted from
# library/sources/NCD20.29-HBO.txt.
#
# Drafted by hand. Covered for the NCD's listed conditions (one question for the fourteen besides diabetic wounds), or
# for a diabetic lower extremity wound meeting all three of its criteria: type 1 or 2 diabetes with a wound due to it,
# Wagner grade III or higher, and an adequate course of standard wound therapy failed (no measurable healing in 30
# days). Every other indication is not covered, so a request with neither is denied. Initial treatment only: the
# NCD's 30-day re-evaluations of continued treatment, and the conditions it excludes by name (each simply not on the
# covered list), are for the reviewer. Questions only: the NCD names no codes for the conditions or the wound grade.
policy hbo
  title "Hyperbaric oxygen therapy (G0277, 99183)"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Medicare NCD 20.29, Hyperbaric Oxygen Therapy: covered conditions; Claims Processing Manual ch. 32, 30.1 for codes"
  status draft
  authority ncd
  lines medicare-advantage medicare
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/hbo
  service hcpcs G0277
  service cpt 99183

evidence covered_condition
  text "One of the NCD's covered conditions: carbon monoxide poisoning, decompression illness, gas embolism, gas gangrene, acute traumatic peripheral ischemia, crush injury or reattached limb, necrotizing fasciitis, acute peripheral arterial insufficiency, compromised skin graft, refractory chronic osteomyelitis, osteoradionecrosis, soft tissue radionecrosis, cyanide poisoning, or refractory actinomycosis"
  clause "Program reimbursement for HBO therapy will be limited to that which is administered in a chamber (including the one man unit) and is limited to the following conditions:"
  find question covered-condition

evidence diabetic_wound
  text "Type 1 or type 2 diabetes with a lower extremity wound due to diabetes"
  clause "Patient has type I or type II diabetes and has a lower extremity wound that is due to diabetes;"
  find question diabetic-wound

evidence wagner_3
  text "The wound is Wagner grade III or higher"
  clause "Patient has a wound classified as Wagner grade III or higher; and"
  find question wagner-3

evidence standard_care_failed
  text "An adequate course of standard wound therapy has failed: no measurable signs of healing in 30 days"
  clause "Patient has failed an adequate course of standard wound therapy."
  find question standard-care-failed
  request document loinc 11506-3

criterion no_diabetic_wound
  text "A diabetic lower extremity wound is not documented."
  clause "Patient has type I or type II diabetes and has a lower extremity wound that is due to diabetes;"
  defeated by diabetic_wound

criterion not_wagner_3
  text "A Wagner grade III or higher wound is not documented."
  clause "Patient has a wound classified as Wagner grade III or higher; and"
  defeated by wagner_3

criterion standard_care_unshown
  text "Failed standard wound therapy is not documented."
  clause "Patient has failed an adequate course of standard wound therapy."
  defeated by standard_care_failed

criterion diabetic_criteria_met
  text "All three diabetic wound criteria are met."
  clause "Diabetic wounds of the lower extremities in patients who meet the following three criteria:"
  defeated by no_diabetic_wound not_wagner_3 standard_care_unshown

criterion no_indication
  text "Neither a covered condition nor a qualifying diabetic wound is documented."
  clause "All other indications not specified under §270.4(A) are not covered under the Medicare program."
  defeated by covered_condition diabetic_criteria_met

criterion indication_shown
  text "A covered condition or a qualifying diabetic wound is documented."
  clause "Program reimbursement for HBO therapy will be limited to that which is administered in a chamber (including the one man unit) and is limited to the following conditions:"
  defeated by no_indication

decision approve approves
  text "Approve hyperbaric oxygen therapy."
  clause "Program reimbursement for HBO therapy will be limited to that which is administered in a chamber (including the one man unit) and is limited to the following conditions:"
  defeated by no_indication

decision deny_not_covered denies
  text "Deny: not a covered condition, and not a diabetic wound meeting all three criteria."
  clause "All other indications not specified under §270.4(A) are not covered under the Medicare program."
  defeated by indication_shown
